{
 "turns": [
  {
   "idx": 0,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Hi, come on in and have a seat. I'm Doctor, Adise Aconquo, one of the cardiologists here. Can you tell me your full name and date of birth?",
   "start": 0.08,
   "end": 9.16
  },
  {
   "idx": 1,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Thomas Weixerach, August 3, 1964.",
   "start": 10.12,
   "end": 13.36
  },
  {
   "idx": 2,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Thank you, Mr. Weixerach. Did you find parking okay? The garage is a mess this week with the construction.",
   "start": 14.3,
   "end": 20.68
  },
  {
   "idx": 3,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Took me two laps, but yeah, I found a spot eventually. Eventually.",
   "start": 21.72,
   "end": 25.24
  },
  {
   "idx": 4,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Sorry about that, so doctor Patel sent you over about some chest discomfort. Tell me what's been going on.",
   "start": 25.76,
   "end": 32.36
  },
  {
   "idx": 5,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "So about six weeks ago I started getting this pressure in the middle of my chest, like somebody's sitting on me. It happens when I walk up the hill to my house, or when I carry groceries up the stairs.",
   "start": 33.1,
   "end": 45.76
  },
  {
   "idx": 6,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "And how long does it last when it comes on?",
   "start": 46.7,
   "end": 48.72
  },
  {
   "idx": 7,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "A few minutes. If I stop and stand there, it goes away in maybe three, four minutes.",
   "start": 49.32,
   "end": 54.68
  },
  {
   "idx": 8,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Does it ever happen when you're resting or wake you up at night?",
   "start": 55.32,
   "end": 58.18
  },
  {
   "idx": 9,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, never at rest, only when I'm pushing it.",
   "start": 59.02,
   "end": 61.9
  },
  {
   "idx": 10,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Does the pressure go anywhere, like your arm, your jaw, or your back?",
   "start": 62.28,
   "end": 65.86
  },
  {
   "idx": 11,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Sometimes a little into my left arm, not the jaw.",
   "start": 66.58,
   "end": 69.66
  },
  {
   "idx": 12,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any shortness of breath with it?",
   "start": 70.54,
   "end": 72.04
  },
  {
   "idx": 13,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "A little winded, yeah. But I figured that's just me being out of shape.",
   "start": 72.5,
   "end": 76.36
  },
  {
   "idx": 14,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any sweating, nausea, or light -headedness with the episodes.",
   "start": 76.36,
   "end": 80.44
  },
  {
   "idx": 15,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No sweating, no nausea, I've never passed out or anything like that.",
   "start": 81.3,
   "end": 85.56
  },
  {
   "idx": 16,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Has it been getting more frequent, or easier to bring on?",
   "start": 86.2,
   "end": 89.06
  },
  {
   "idx": 17,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I'm not really. It's about the same, maybe two or three times a week.",
   "start": 89.66,
   "end": 93.76
  },
  {
   "idx": 18,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Okay, doctor. Patel's note says you have high blood pressure and high cholesterol. What are you taking for those?",
   "start": 94.28,
   "end": 101.0
  },
  {
   "idx": 19,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Listen, April, 20 milligrams in the morning. And he started me on Ador Vastatin, 40 milligrams at night, about a year ago.",
   "start": 101.94,
   "end": 110.48
  },
  {
   "idx": 20,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any allergies to medications?",
   "start": 111.23,
   "end": 112.51
  },
  {
   "idx": 21,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Penicillin. I got hives from it as a kid.",
   "start": 113.37,
   "end": 115.93
  },
  {
   "idx": 22,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Do you smoke?",
   "start": 116.79,
   "end": 117.27
  },
  {
   "idx": 23,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I quit ten years ago. Before that, I smoked about a pack a day for twenty -five years.",
   "start": 118.21,
   "end": 123.51
  },
  {
   "idx": 24,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Good for you on quitting, that's a big deal. Any diabetes?",
   "start": 124.35,
   "end": 127.17
  },
  {
   "idx": 25,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, my sugar's always been fine.",
   "start": 128.37,
   "end": 130.41
  },
  {
   "idx": 26,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "And what do you do for work?",
   "start": 131.13,
   "end": 132.15
  },
  {
   "idx": 27,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I'm a dispatcher at Hollister Freight, mostly sitting honestly.",
   "start": 132.73,
   "end": 136.67
  },
  {
   "idx": 28,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Okay, your blood pressure today is 142 over 86, pulse 74, and your oxygen is 98%. Weight is 214 pounds. Let me take a listen. Heart has a regular rhythm, no murmurs. Lungs are clear. No swelling in your legs and the pulses in your feet are good.",
   "start": 137.57,
   "end": 156.61
  },
  {
   "idx": 29,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "That's good, I guess. Yes.",
   "start": 157.43,
   "end": 158.63
  },
  {
   "idx": 30,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "We did an ECG when you came in. It shows normal sinus rhythm at 72, and I don't see any signs of an old heart attack or any acute changes. That's reassuring, but arresting ECG is often normal even when there's a blockage, because the problem only shows up when the heart is working hard.",
   "start": 159.11,
   "end": 177.89
  },
  {
   "idx": 31,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "So what does that mean then?",
   "start": 178.55,
   "end": 179.91
  },
  {
   "idx": 32,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "What you're describing, pressure with exertion that goes away with rest, is pretty classic for stable angina. That means the heart muscle isn't getting enough blood when it works harder, usually from narrowing in the heart arteries. With your smoking history, blood pressure and cholesterol, that's my main concern.",
   "start": 180.5,
   "end": 198.96
  },
  {
   "idx": 33,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay, that's kind of scary.",
   "start": 199.64,
   "end": 201.04
  },
  {
   "idx": 34,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I understand. The good news is it's stable, and we have a clear plan. First, I'd like you to have a nuclear stress test where you walk on a treadmill while we take pictures of the blood flow to your heart. will also check a fasting lipid panel and a basic metabolic panel.",
   "start": 202.04,
   "end": 218.2
  },
  {
   "idx": 35,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Sure, that's fine.",
   "start": 218.82,
   "end": 219.82
  },
  {
   "idx": 36,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "In the meantime, I want you to start aspirin, 81 milligrams once a day. I'm also starting Metoprolol 6 and 8, 25 milligrams once a day, which slows the heart down so it doesn't work as hard. And I'm giving you nitroglycerin, 0 .4 milligrams, one tablet under the tongue if the pressure comes on and doesn't go away with rest. You can repeat it every five minutes up to three tablets.",
   "start": 220.71,
   "end": 245.05
  },
  {
   "idx": 37,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Got it.",
   "start": 245.81,
   "end": 246.39
  },
  {
   "idx": 38,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I'm also going to increase your atorvastatin from 40 to 80 milligrams at night. Keep the lisinopril the same.",
   "start": 246.93,
   "end": 254.35
  },
  {
   "idx": 39,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay.",
   "start": 254.95,
   "end": 255.35
  },
  {
   "idx": 40,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Now this part is important. If you get chest pain at rest, or pain that lasts more than 15 minutes, or it doesn't go away after one nitroglycerin, call 911. Don't drive yourself.",
   "start": 256.07,
   "end": 268.95
  },
  {
   "idx": 41,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Understood. Good.",
   "start": 270.05,
   "end": 270.75
  },
  {
   "idx": 42,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "And hold off on heavy lifting and that hill until we have the stress test results. What's the best number to reach you for scheduling?",
   "start": 271.41,
   "end": 278.99
  },
  {
   "idx": 43,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "My cell 555 -0163.",
   "start": 279.73,
   "end": 281.97
  },
  {
   "idx": 44,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Great. We'll get the stress test done within the next two weeks, and I'll see you back right after to go over the results.",
   "start": 283.55,
   "end": 290.07
  },
  {
   "idx": 45,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Thanks, Doctor. I appreciate it.",
   "start": 290.91,
   "end": 292.95
  }
 ],
